  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afb5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5140,
      "bookHadithIndex": 101,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Asma' Ar-Rahabi that Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah [SAW], told him:\"Fatimah bint Hubairah came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] with a big ring on her hand.\" He (the narrator) said: \"This is what I found in the book of my father, a huge ring.\"- \"The Messenger of Allah [SAW] started hitting her hand, so she entered upon Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah [SAW], and complained to her about what the Messenger of Allah [SAW] had done. Fatimah took off a gold chain from her neck and said: 'This was given to me by Abu Hasan.' The Messenger of Allah [SAW] came in and (ﷺ) the chain in her hand. He said: 'O Fatimah, would you like the people to say that the daughter of the Messenger of Allah [SAW] has a chain of fire in her hand?' Then he went out, without sitting down. Fatimah sent the chain to the market and sold it, and she bought a slave with the money, and set him free. He was told of that and he said: 'Praise be to Allah, Who has saved Fatimah from the Fire",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5140-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5140-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5140-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afb6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5141,
      "bookHadithIndex": 102,
      "text": "It was narrated that Thawban said:\"The daughter of Hubairah came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and on her hand were large gold rings.\" - a similar report",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5141-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5141-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afb7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5142,
      "bookHadithIndex": 103,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\"I was sitting with the Prophet [SAW] when a woman came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, two bracelets of gold.' He said: 'Two bracelets of fire.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a necklace of gold.' He said: 'A necklace of fire.' She said: 'Two earrings of gold.' He said: 'Two earrings of fire.' She was wearing two bracelets of gold, so she took them off and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if a woman does not adorn herself for her husband, she will become unattractive to him.' He said: 'What is there to keep any one of you from making earrings of silver and painting them yellow with saffron or some 'Abir'?' This is the wording of Ibn Harb",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5142-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5142-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5142-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afb8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5143,
      "bookHadithIndex": 104,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] saw her wearing two bracelets of gold. The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: \"Shall I not tell you of something that is better than this? Why don't you take these off and wear two bracelets of silver, and paint them yellow with saffron, and they will look fine",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5143-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5143-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5143-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afb9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5144,
      "bookHadithIndex": 105,
      "text": "Ali bin Abi Talib said:\"The Prophet of Allah [SAW] took hold of some silk in his right hand and some gold in his left, then he said: 'These two are forbidden for the males of my Ummah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5144-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5144-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5144-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afba",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5145,
      "bookHadithIndex": 106,
