          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Maqtu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5185-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afe3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5186,
      "bookHadithIndex": 147,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\"The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade me to wear gold rings",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5186-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5186-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5186-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afe4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5187,
      "bookHadithIndex": 148,
      "text": "Hafs Al-Laithi said:\"I bear witness that 'Imran narrated to us, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] forbade wearing silk, and gold rings, and drinking from Al-Hanatim",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5187-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5187-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5187-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afe5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5188,
      "bookHadithIndex": 149,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that:A man came from Najran to the Messenger of Allah [SAW]. He was wearing a gold ring, and the Messenger of Allah [SAW] turned away from him, and said: \"You have come to me with a coal of fire on your hand",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5188-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5188-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5188-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c6d6dd1a4c9c86f0afe6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 48,
      "hadithIndex": 5189,
      "bookHadithIndex": 150,
      "text": "It was narrated from Al-Bara' bin 'Azib that :A man was sitting with the Prophet [SAW] and he was wearing a gold ring. The Messenger of Allah [SAW] had a stick in his hand and the Prophet [SAW] struck his finger. The man said: \"What's wrong with me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Why don't you get rid of this thing that is on your finger?\" The man took it and threw it away. The Prophet [SAW] saw him after that and said: \"What happened to the ring?\" He said: \"I threw it away.\" He said: \"I did not tell you to do that, rather I told you to sell it and benefit from its price.\" This Hadith is Munkar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5189-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5189-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-48-5189-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
